.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt FILEES-MAIL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-mail
.Nd submit one FileES outbox entry or drain Public Shares mail
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm send
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm public-loop
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Cm send
claims one pending control-plane mail job and submits it through the
configured SMTP relay.
It is the one-shot drain used after
.Xr filees-admin 8
ticket actions and after
.Xr filees-bootstrap-entry 8 .
Onboarding, realm-removal, data-erasure and upload-shelf invitation jobs
share this path.
.Pp
Delivery states are
.Cm pending ,
.Cm sending ,
.Cm queued ,
and
.Cm failed .
A 4xx leaves the job
.Cm pending
and preserves the OTP.
A 5xx marks an onboarding job
.Cm failed
and redacts the OTP.
An upload-shelf invitation 5xx marks the outbox job
.Cm failed
without retry, so
.Cm public-loop
does not hammer the relay.
The invitation token remains on the channel record.
The
.Ic Message-ID
is derived from
.Ic CreatedAt ,
so a lost 250 can be retried safely.
.Pp
.Cm public-loop
is not an operator command.
.Xr filees-public-authority 8
supervises it as an isolated child.
The child loads the SMTP secret and drains the Public Shares outbox and
the upload-shelf invitation outbox.
The authority process never receives that secret.
If the child dies, the authority exits.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 4n -compact
.It 0
accepted
.Pq Cm queued
or nothing pending
.It 75
temporary SMTP failure; retry
.It 69
permanent SMTP failure; the job is marked failed, not retried
.It 65
message render failure; the job is marked failed, not retried
.It 64, 78, 70
usage, configuration or internal error
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Retry a 4xx invitation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-mail send
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees-admin 8 ,
.Xr filees-bootstrap-entry 8 ,
.Xr filees-public-authority 8
